Date: Wed, 22 Apr 2026 12:28:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/23] testsuite: Add Bugzilla reporter attribution to
 pr123868.f90 [PR fortran/123868]

Retrospective attribution header added as part of a manual
Bugzilla-provenance audit on 2026-04-22 (meta-repo tracking commit
40f0a94; GitHub issues on krystophny/gcc-dev).  The existing GCC
Fortran testsuite convention (see pr113363.f90, pdt_50.f03,
arrayio_4.f90) uses an in-file "! Contributed by ..." line; practice
is inconsistent and attribution is not strictly required for small
Bugzilla reducers, but we are adding it retroactively for provenance
safety and completeness.  No behavioural change.

Assisted-by: Claude (Anthropic)
Assisted-by: GPT (OpenAI)

	PR fortran/123868

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gfortran.dg/pr123868.f90: Add reporter attribution header.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
---
 gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/pr123868.f90 | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/pr123868.f90 b/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/pr123868.f90
index e21501ddacc..d5ce947f3e3 100644
--- a/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/pr123868.f90
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gfortran.dg/pr123868.f90
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 ! { dg-do run }
 ! PR fortran/123868 - Memory leak on assignment with nested allocatable
+! Contributed by Andrew Benson  <abensonca@gcc.gnu.org>
 ! components.  Regression introduced by PR121628 commit which caused
 ! gfc_duplicate_allocatable to be called twice for allocatable array
 ! components with nested allocatable components.
